// Regla Sigma: proc_creation_win_sc_query_interesting_services.yml
// ID Sigma: e83e8899-c9b2-483b-b355-5decc942b959
// Título: Interesting Service Enumeration Via Sc.EXE
// Descripción: Detects the enumeration and query of interesting and in some cases sensitive services on the system via "sc.exe".
Attackers often try to enumerate the services currently running on a system in order to find different attack vectors.

// Aplica a: Producto: windows | Categoría: process_creation
// Producto: windows
// Categoría: process_creation
// Servicio: 
// Nivel: low
// Pipeline: microsoft_xdr
// Ruta original: C:\SigmaLab\sigma\rules\windows\process_creation\proc_creation_win_sc_query_interesting_services.yml
// Requiere validación en el entorno de destino.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\sc.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "sc.exe") and ProcessCommandLine contains "query" and ProcessCommandLine contains "termservice"
